      "_purpose": "Google's open-source Google Ads MCP server (Apache-2.0). Tools: list_accessible_customers, search (GAQL), get_resource_metadata. Google: 'This implementation is strictly read-only. It cannot modify bids, pause campaigns, or create new assets.' Use it for audits, pacing and reporting; Google Ads writes still go through a write-capable connector behind the approval gate.",
      "_local_stdio_alternative": "Default mode is local stdio, Claude Code only (not Cowork): {\"command\": \"pipx\", \"args\": [\"run\", \"--spec\", \"google-ads-mcp==<pinned-version>\", \"google-ads-mcp\"]}. The server switches to Streamable HTTP when its OAuth-proxy environment variables are set (self-hosting, e.g. Cloud Run) — that is the URL form above.",
